{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The equation of a scaled\n transformation of the graph of $f(x)=x^2$ can have the form:\n\n$g(x)=\\green{a}x^2$\n\nIf $|\\green{a}|\u003e1$, the graph is stretched vertically, and if $|\\green{a}|\u003c1$, the graph is compressed vertically.\n\nWhen $\\green{a}\u003c0$, the parabola is then reflected across the $x$-axis.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's compare corresponding points in $\\blueD{f}$ and $\\maroonD{g}$. For example, $\\blueD{f}(4)=16$ and $\\maroonD{g}(4)=8$.\n\n$\\dfrac{8}{16}=0.5$\n\nEach $y$-coordinate in $\\maroonD{g}$ is $0.5$ times the distance from the $x$-axis as the corresponding $y$-coordinate in $\\blueD{f}$.  \n\nSo, $\\greenD{a}=0.5$.\n\n[[☃ interaction 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"interaction 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"elements":[{"key":"function-ab44e3","options":{"color":"#6495ED","funcName":"f","rangeMax":"10","rangeMin":"-10","strokeDasharray":"","strokeWidth":3,"value":"x^2"},"type":"function"},{"key":"function-b966e4","options":{"color":"#FF00AF","funcName":"g","rangeMax":"10","rangeMin":"-10","strokeDasharray":"- ","strokeWidth":3,"value":"0.5\\cdot x^2"},"type":"function"},{"key":"movable-point-66232f","options":{"constraint":"none","constraintFn":"0","constraintXMax":"5","constraintXMin":"-5","constraintYMax":"0","constraintYMin":"0","snap":0.5,"startX":"2","startY":"0","varSubscript":0},"type":"movable-point"},{"key":"line-913209","options":{"arrows":"","color":"#28AE7B","endX":"x_0","endY":"f\\left(x_0\\right)","startX":"x_0","startY":"0","strokeDasharray":"- ","strokeWidth":3},"type":"line"},{"key":"line-b63598","options":{"arrows":"","color":"#28AE7B","endX":"0","endY":"g\\left(x_0\\right)","startX":"x_0","startY":"g\\left(x_0\\right)","strokeDasharray":"","strokeWidth":3},"type":"line"},{"key":"line-fff428","options":{"arrows":"","color":"#28AE7B","endX":"0","endY":"f\\left(x_0\\right)","startX":"x_0","startY":"f\\left(x_0\\right)","strokeDasharray":"","strokeWidth":3},"type":"line"}],"graph":{"backgroundImage":{"height":0,"url":null,"width":0},"box":[300,300],"editableSettings":["canvas","graph"],"gridStep":[1,1],"labels":["x","y"],"markings":"graph","range":[[-5,5],[-1,9]],"rulerLabel":"","rulerTicks":10,"showProtractor":false,"showRuler":false,"showTooltips":false,"snapStep":[1,1],"tickStep":[1,1],"valid":true},"static":false},"static":false,"type":"interaction","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion,\n\n$g(x)=0.5x^2$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Function $g$ can be thought of as a scaled version of $f(x)=x^2$.\n\n![A parabola labeled f represents the equation y equals x squared. A parabola labeled g passes through the point negative 4, 8, through the origin, and through the point 4, 8.](web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/ca0f06d54ebea47e61c195a31a1661101cbbfa2d)\n\n**Write the equation for $g(x)$.**\n\n$g(x)=$ [[☃ expression 1]]","images":{"web+graphie:${☣ LOCALPATH}/images/ca0f06d54ebea47e61c195a31a1661101cbbfa2d":{"height":325,"width":325}},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"0.5x^2"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
